    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/creative-media-producer-and-editor-iii-530690-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Creative Media Producer and Editor III",
      "description": "Creative Media Producer and Editor III - 530690 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Creative Media Producer and Editor III - 530690 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Creative Media Producer and Editor III - 530690 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Graphic Design/Web Design Other Closing at: Oct 8 2026 - 22:55 CDT Add to favorites View favorites Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $53,500 - Midpoint: $66,900 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 301203 - Marketing & Brand Strategy-Strategi Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some evenings & weekends as necessary Job Summary: The Creative Media Producer and Editor III produces a variety of visual storytelling content for the University through creative, digital, and traditional media under minimal supervision to promote and publicize the university, its entities, and administrators to all stakeholders with a particular focus on university branding, storytelling, and recruitment and retention of students. Creates, manages, and executes visual storytelling productions for high-visibility projects tied to the University's strategic vision. Works directly with clients to review and approve projects and prepare them for deployment. Provides training, guidance, and/or supervision to other Creative Media Producer and Editors. Additional Department Summary: Creates compelling video content to support key strategic partners across the institution with a particular emphasis on undergraduate recruitment and fundraising. Engages in high-level video productions, including the annual institutional television commercial, and works to creatively influence the visual look of the UA brand. Shoots and edits video content of campus events (homecoming, commencement, etc.) Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in broadcast communication, telecommunication and film, journalism, or graphic design and four (4) years of broadcast, multimedia production, communications, and/or media relations experience; OR master's degree in broadcast communication, telecommunication and film, journalism, or graphic design and two (2) years of broadcast, multimedia production, communications, and/or media relations experience. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: This position may work night and/or weekends. Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. A portfolio, reel, or links to relevant video work samples will be requested. Skills and Knowledge: Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate with internal and external partners. Proficiency in shooting and editing a variety of video content. In-depth knowledge of industry-standard video equipment, cinematography, storytelling, lighting techniques, and conducting interviews. Comprehensive knowledge of Premiere Pro and working knowledge of Adobe After Effects and Adobe Photoshop. Understanding of social media platforms, including effectively utilizing video content on these platforms. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Canon cinema cameras, tripods, gimbals, audio, and studio equipment. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 517cc49f Last Name (required) a68e3ce5 Email (required) 7b509a8b Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. ea724350 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Graphic Design/Web Design Other Graphic Design/Web Design Other Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) d4df1fb6 Last Name (required) d655bfb9 Email (required) 908e4526 Friend's Information 1833b375 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) b41a3c2d Last Name (required) 0300bffb Email (required)