    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/accountant-i-530909-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Accountant I",
      "description": "Accountant I - 530909 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Accountant I - 530909 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Accountant I - 530909 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Accounting/Bookkeeping Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 22:55 CDT Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $49,100 - Midpoint: $61,400 (Salaried E7) Department/Organization: 502702 - Campus Financial Affairs Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Accountant I prepares, reconciles, and audits budgets under general supervision. Prepares financial reports, invoices, schedules, and/or statements. Completes journal entries. Reviews, analyzes, and approves expenditures. Determines fund balances. Ensures compliance with applicable laws, University policies, and procedures. Additional Department Summary: Supports the Office of Information Technology's (OIT) financial operations by compiling monthly budget reports for leadership review, conducting financial analyses, and preparing reports for external entities. Manages departmental budgets, oversees monthly procurement activity exceeding $1 million, maintains the purchasing ledger, and ensures compliance with University financial policies and procedures. Reviews transactions for proper authorization. Prepares tax reports and federal credit calculations. Maintains digital financial records. Serves as the audit liaison for construction projects. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree or higher in Accounting, Finance, Business, or related financial field. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Banner, IBM TM1, and Concur. Experience in an institution of higher education and understanding of related organizatio