p with the Alabama Entrepreneurship Institute, The EDGE, and other entrepreneurship programs. Applicants must demonstrate the ability to be an active and engaged member of a highly collaborative faculty team. The successful hire will teach four courses each fall and spring semester and may teach master's and doctoral courses, depending on academic qualifications. Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications for consideration for assistant professor rank ● A terminal degree in public relations or a related field (Ph.D.) and at least three years of professional experience in public relations or a related field, including at least one year involving entrepreneurial communications activities. ● Proficiency in AP style ● Previous teaching experience is not required. Minimum Qualifications for consideration for associate professor rank ● A terminal degree in public relations or a related field (Ph.D.) and at least 10 years of professional experience in public relations or a related field, including at least three years involving entrepreneurial communications activities. ● Proficiency in AP style ● Previous teaching experience is not required. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications (for either rank) ● Five years or more of public relations experience in senior or leadership roles ● Three years or more of leadership-level entrepreneurial communications activities. ● Experience teaching college-level classes or experience leading employee training or workshops o We are especially interested in candidates who have used innovative, experiential approaches to teaching, such as client-based projects, design thinking, venture simulations, pitch development, and interdisciplinary collaboration, and who can help students develop the creativity, adaptability, and comfort with experimentation that entrepreneurial environments demand. ● Experience working with AI to assist with or create public relations communications. Instructions and Required Materials for Application 