    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/high-performance-computing-data-storage-administrator-i-530898-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator I",
      "description": "High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator I - 530898 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator I - 530898 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator I - 530898 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Nov 5 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $69,200 - Midpoint: $89,900 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 200706 - OIT-HPC Center Services Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator I assists with the administration of enterprise and high-performance computing (HPC) storage systems. Monitors storage health, capacity, availability, and hardware and assists with routine maintenance, upgrades, provisioning, and filesystem expansion. Assists with administering distributed and parallel filesystems, managing project storage allocations, configuring quotas and permissions, and supporting metadata management. Performs backups, recovery operations, archive workflows, data migrations, and lifecycle activities. Monitors utilization and input/output performance, identifies potential bottlenecks, and assists with filesystem tuning. Develops and maintains Bash and Python scripts to automate provisioning and monitoring tasks. Troubleshoots storage and file access issues and assists researchers and technical staff with data management. Additional Department Summary: Provides operational and technical support for the University's high-performance computing (HPC) storage infrastructure. Works with system administrators and application administrators to ensure reliable, secure, and high-performance access to research data across multi-petabyte storage systems. Assists with storage administration, user support, data lifecycle management, and performance monitoring. Develops expertise in enterprise-scale HPC storage technologies. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and four (4) years of systems administration or storage administration experience; OR associate's degree and two (2) years of systems administration or storage administration experience; OR bachelor's degree and some systems administration or storage administration experience; OR master's degree. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Understanding of filesystems and storage concepts. Familiarity with networking fundamentals. Strong troubleshooting skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in computer science, information systems, data science, or a related computational discipline. One (1) year of Linux systems administration or storage administration experience. Experience with Linux command line. Experience supporting research users. Experience with Linux, Bash, Python, GPFS, DataCore Ngenea, PowerScale, PowerScale Archive, NFS, DMB, SSH, Git, Ansible, Globus, VMWare or virtualization, object storage, or other data transfer tools. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) add52bd6 Last Name (required) 6f2c0923 Email (required) 7d57b8ae Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 470380b2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Systems/Technology Support Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 5db36c61 Last Name (required) 5c8af7b0 Email (required) c932ebd3 Friend's Information d84ba57c Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are