    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/systems-analyst-iii-530872-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst III",
      "description": "Systems Analyst III - 530872 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Systems Analyst III - 530872 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Systems Analyst III - 530872 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Oct 27 2026 - 22:55 CDT Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $62,800 - Midpoint: $81,700 (Salaried E10) Department/Organization: 200721 - Enterprise Technology Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Systems Analyst III plans and configures moderate- to high-complexity software systems to support the administrative function of the University under minimal supervision. This may include enterprise and highly critical critical applications. Assists in the development of processes. Creates workflows. Installs, configures, supports, and maintains integrations for vendor-supplied software systems. Works on a team and collaborates with specific departments, colleges, and customers around campus. Supports their needs, troubleshooting and resolving issues, and responding to their questions and concerns in a timely manner. Provides guidance and training to other Systems Analysts. Additional Department Summary: This senior position, under minimal supervision, administers and supports moderate- to high-complexity University-managed cloud applications, including traditional cloud / SaaS applications as well as artificial intelligence (AI) platforms such as Anthropic, OpenAI ChatGPT, Microsoft, and Google Gemini. This position works with cloud systems engineers to manage Azure and Google GCP environments. Independently manages platform configuration, identity and access functions, enterprise licensing, audit and usage reporting, application lifecycle activities, and non-routine technical troubleshooting. Plans and executes approved migrations of accounts, workspaces, projects, content, histories, and configurations; supports single sign-on, automated provisioning, directory synchronization, and application programming interface integrations; tests platform changes; and coordinates technical resolution with users, vendors, and University teams. Provides guidance and training to other Systems Analysts. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree and two (2) years of IT system analysis experience; OR bachelor's degree and four (4) years of IT system analysis experience; OR associate's degree and six (6) years of IT experience to include four (4) years of IT system analysis; OR high school diploma or GED and eight (8) years of IT experience to include four (4) years of IT system analysis. Skills and Knowledge: Considerable knowledge of cloud application administration, identity and access management, role-based access control, enterprise licensing, tenant or organization configuration, single sign-on, multifactor authentication, automated provisioning, audit logs, application programming interfaces (APIs), integrations, and software-as-a-service lifecycle practices. Ability to plan and execute account, content, workspace, history, and configuration migrations using vendor-supported methods; develop inventories, mappings, test plans, validation procedures, communications, rollback steps, and exception remediation. Skill in diagnosing non-routine authentication, authorization, entitlement, data-transfer, configuration, integration, and vendor-dependency problems across multiple services. Ability to interpret vendor documentation, logs, audit events, reports, structured data, and release notices; communicate risk and status; train analysts and users; and manage multiple technical assignments through completion. Strong understanding of security, privacy, records-management, procurement, accessibility, contractual, and responsible AI requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Four (4) years of experience supporting or administering cloud applications, enterprise software-as-a-service platforms, identity and access management, application integrations, or comparable IT systems. Experience independently troubleshooting application issues, analyzing logs or administrative reports, performing migrations or implementations, documenting technical processes, and coordinating work with customers, vendors, or technical teams. Experience serving as an administrator for multiple enterprise cloud applications or AI platforms, including Anthropic, OpenAI ChatGPT, Microsoft cloud and AI services, or Google Gemini. Experience with Microsoft Azure or Google GCP. Experience with tenant or organization administration, identity federation, single sign-on, automated provisioning, directory synchronization, APIs, scripting, data export and import, content migration, audit and usage analytics, vendor escalation, and change management. Experience supporting higher education environments. Relevant cloud, identity, security, data, or vendor certifications. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 359dc8e5 Last Name (required) 554a542d Email (required) 62db419d Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. fb0ca4d7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Systems/Technology Support Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 5a0a902a Last Name (required) 6a13a337 Email (required) ee5ca24e Friend's Information 535b965f Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) bcc77ca6 Last Name (required) bc34e563 Email (required) 124ce2e2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate