    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/systems-analyst-iv-530873-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Systems Analyst IV",
      "description": "Systems Analyst IV - 530873 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Systems Analyst IV - 530873 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Systems Analyst IV - 530873 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Oct 27 2026 - 22:55 CDT Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $69,200 - Midpoint: $89,900 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 200721 - Enterprise Technology Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Systems Analyst IV plans and configures high-complexity software systems to support the administrative function of the University under minimal supervision. This may include enterprise and highly critical applications. Assists in the development of processes. Creates workflows. Installs, configures, supports, and maintains integrations for vendor-supplied software systems. Works on a team and collaborates with specific departments, colleges, and customers around campus. Supports their needs, troubleshooting and resolving issues, and responding to their questions and concerns in a timely manner. Provides guidance, training, and/or supervision to other Systems Analysts. Additional Department Summary: This senior-level subject matter expert, under minimal supervision, leads the design, optimization, integration, sustainment, and advisory support of high-complexity, enterprise University cloud applications, including artificial intelligence (AI) platforms such as Anthropic, OpenAI ChatGPT, Microsoft, and Google Gemini. This position works with cloud systems engineers to manage Azure and Google GCP environments. Establishes technical service models, account and access structures, delegated-administration boundaries, lifecycle practices, integration approaches, migration strategies, support standards, and roadmaps. Leads complex implementations, consolidations, migrations, integrations, and root-cause analysis; evaluates vendor changes and service risks; and advises University units on supportable platform use, configuration, access, data handling, and operational practices. Coordinates institution-wide work with security, privacy, procurement, legal, records-management, accessibility, identity, architecture, vendors, and functional stakeholders. Provides guidance, training, and/or supervision to other Systems Analysts. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree and four (4) years of IT system analysis experience; OR bachelor's degree and six (6) years of IT system analysis experience; OR associate's degree and eight (8) years of IT experience to include six (6) years of IT system analysis; OR high school diploma or GED and ten (10) years of IT experience to include six (6) years of IT system analysis. Skills and Knowledge: Advanced knowledge of enterprise cloud application administration, identity and access management, role-based access control, delegated administration, enterprise licensing, tenant or organization configuration, audit logging, APIs, integrations, data migration, service lifecycle management, and vendor support processes. Ability to translate business, technical, security, privacy, accessibility, records, procurement, contractual, and responsible AI requirements into supportable service designs, controls, standards, migration strategies, implementation plans, and operating models. Expert skill in resolving complex cross-platform issues involving authentication, authorization, provisioning, content, integrations, data flows, configuration, and vendor dependencies. Ability to evaluate alternatives, constraints, risks, and total support impact and present clear recommendations to technical and non-technical audiences. Ability to lead projects, coordinate stakeholders, mentor or supervise analysts, develop roadmaps and documentation, and make sound decisions with minimal supervision. Preferred Qualifications: Six (6) years of experience supporting or administering cloud applications, enterprise software-as-a-service platforms, identity and access management, application integrations, or comparable IT systems, including experience leading complex migrations, implementations, integrations, troubleshooting, or technical projects. Experience advising customers or leadership on technical solutions, service design, operational risk, governance controls, or technology adoption. Experience serving as a senior administrator, technical lead, service owner, architect, or consultant for enterprise cloud applications or AI platforms, including Anthropic, OpenAI ChatGPT, Microsoft cloud and AI services, or Google Gemini. Experience with Microsoft Azure or Google GCP. Experience with enterprise agreements, tenant consolidation, complex content migrations, identity federation, automated provisioning, APIs, scripting, audit and usage analytics, governance, service design, roadmap development, and institution-wide implementations. Experience advising distributed higher education units on enterprise technology adoption. Relevant advanced cloud, identity, security, architecture, data, service-management, project-management, or vendor certifications. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) ce41130f Last Name (required) 432e02cc Email (required) 7042bf14 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 421e5772 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Systems/Technology Support Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) b22be586 Last Name (required) b656f0a0 Email (required) f549f9a9 Friend's Information d1fdeff0 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 21f2ba84 Last Name (required) 1554751e Email (required) 5a6eea91 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You