    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/purchasing-assistant-530867-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Purchasing Assistant",
      "description": "Purchasing Assistant - 530867 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Purchasing Assistant - 530867 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Purchasing Assistant - 530867 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Other Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 22:55 CDT Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $16.78 - Midpoint: $20.14 (Hourly N3) Department/Organization: 200701 - Information Technology Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Purchasing Assistant aides in procurement-related activities at the college or University level. Additional Department Summary: Provides technology procurement and purchasing support for faculty, staff, departments, and administrative units served by the Office of Information Technology (OIT). Responsible for coordinating the procurement lifecycle for end-user computing devices, peripherals, software, and other technology-related purchases supporting academic, research, instructional, and administrative operations. Serves as a central resource for technology purchasing activities, ensuring compliance with University purchasing policies and procedures. Works closely with departmental customers, vendors, Central Purchasing, Central Receiving, and technical support teams to facilitate efficient acquisition, payment reconciliation, receipt, and distribution of technology equipment. Supports the University's technology lifecycle management program through the maintenance of procurement, inventory, and asset management records and by assisting with the administration of enterprise IT asset management systems and processes. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. Skills and Knowledge: Effective communication skills. Ability to work in a team environment. Ability to multi-task and complete assigned tasks on time with limited supervision. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with UA procurement policies and procedures, budget environment, and working in Banner. Experience using Microsoft Excel. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 5521d860 Last Name (required) bad94941 Email (required) 609bb4e0 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 2eec7388 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the c