    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/scholar-development-coordinator-530866-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Scholar Development Coordinator",
      "description": "Scholar Development Coordinator - 530866 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Scholar Development Coordinator - 530866 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Scholar Development Coordinator - 530866 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Advising/Peer Support Program Coordination Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 22:55 CDT Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $49,100 - Midpoint: $61,400 (Salaried E7) Department/Organization: 200023 - The Office of Undergraduate Edu Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Scholar Development Coordinator assists with student mentorship, scholar development programming, campus engagement, and advising initiatives within the Office of External Scholarships and Fellowships (OESF). Develops and implements scholar development initiatives that prepare students for competitive opportunities throughout their undergraduate careers. Collaborates with faculty and staff to identify, mentor, and develop students with academic, leadership, research, service, and professional potential while expanding awareness of nationally competitive scholarships, fellowships, graduate education, prestigious internships, and other high-impact opportunities across the University. Additional Department Summary: Coordinates workshops, mentoring initiatives, outreach efforts, and partnerships with academic colleges, faculty, advisors, and campus organizations to cultivate broad participation, strengthen the University's scholar pipeline, and expand equitable access to transformative educational opportunities. Provides individualized mentoring and developmental advising, creates educational programming, tracks student engagement and outcomes, and contributes to the strategic growth of OESF and its university-wide mission. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of experience; OR master's degree and some experience. Skills and Knowledge: Knowledge of undergraduate student development, high-impact educational practices, nationally competitive scholarships, fellowships, graduate education, undergraduate research, and related opportunities. Ability to develop educational programming that supports student growth, leadership, and academic success. Ability to multi-task and coordinate multiple projects and priorities while maintaining exceptional attention to detail. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, administrators, alumni, and external partners. Exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and provide outstanding student service. Strong interpersonal skills and a positive, collaborative, and professional work ethic. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree and two (2) years of relevant professional experience in higher education involving student development, advising, honors education, nationally prestigious scholarships and fellowships, undergraduate education and/or teaching, academic affairs, experiential learning, or a closely related area; OR bachelor's degree and six (6) years of progressively responsible professional experience in one or more of these areas. Experience advising, mentoring, or supporting college students. Experience with nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships, honors education, scholar development, undergraduate research, undergraduate teaching, or student success initiatives, mentoring students for graduate school, internships, research opportunities, or competitive academic programs. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 9afba5c6 Last Name (required) 75e459a9 Email (required) 27b6257d Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 030c267f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Advising/Peer Support Program Coordination Advising/Peer Support Program Coordination Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) cfcaff86 Last Name (required) 801457b8 Email (required) cfd1d45d Friend's Information 291dadee Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 d