    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/workday-business-analyst-i-hcm-530809-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Workday Business Analyst I",
      "description": "Workday Business Analyst I - HCM - 530809 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Workday Business Analyst I - HCM - 530809 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Workday Business Analyst I - HCM - 530809 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Human Resources Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Nov 7 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $62,800 - Midpoint: $81,700 (Salaried E10) Department/Organization: 506152 - Compensation Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am - 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Workday Business Analyst I assists in gathering and documenting business requirements, user stories, and process descriptions for Workday configuration and security activities. Creates and maintains process documentation, workflow diagrams, and meeting notes under the direction of senior team members. Performs data entry, data validation, and basic data analysis tasks in support of Workday application management activities. Supports cross-functional coordination efforts by maintaining shared team resources and documentation repositories. Assists in coordinating meetings, tracking action items, and following up with stakeholders on outstanding deliverables. Works closely with functional teams to ensure accurate and timely provisioning in alignment with institutional access controls. Additional Department Summary: The Workday Business Analyst I supports the administration, configuration, maintenance, and continuous improvement of the Workday platform. This position assists with business analysis, requirements documentation, system support, testing, reporting, and process improvement activities while developing knowledge of Workday functionality, organizational business processes, and business analysis methodologies. Working under general supervision and guidance, the analyst assists with evaluating business needs, troubleshooting system issues, implementing approved configuration changes, and supporting Workday enhancements. The position follows established governance, security, and change control processes and maintains a strong customer service focus to ensure a positive user experience. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher and some experience supporting or working with Workday or similar Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems. Skills and Knowledge: Workday workstream areas may include: Core HR, Identity Management, Talent & Performance, Learning, Position Management, Compensation, Absence, and/or Time Tracking. Foundational knowledge of business analysis principles and methodologies. Strong customer service orientation and interpersonal skills. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Analytical and problem-solving abilities. Ability to learn complex business processes and technologies. Basic understanding of ERP systems and SaaS applications. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Understanding of change management and documentation practices. Preferred Qualifications: Two (2) years of professional work experience in business analysis, customer support, systems support, human resources, finance, operations, information technology, project coordination, or a related business function. Experience supporting, using, or working with enterprise applications, ERP systems, SaaS platforms, or other business systems. Experience gathering information, documenting processes, analyzing data, or resolving user issues. Experience working in a higher education, healthcare, government, or large complex organizational environment. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) c3f591ac Last Name (required) 33d14062 Email (required) 5be9b680 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. f669b841 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Information Systems/Technology Support Human Resources Information Systems/Technology Support Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 832e25c5 Last Name (required) bab3e06a Email (required) 8447e51b Fri